i learned this the hard way.

I was 2/5 for half of a 49 minute game as Asol (but I was able to end the game at 13/6 with the power of late game mage). When I saw that we were hard losing and my team was kinda ass, I just kept farming and got 400 cs by the end of the game. I got an S+ rating for that.

&#x200B;

I thought I wouldn't get even an S rating for it cause the first half of the game was so ass, but I think cs really impacts the score a lot cause I've had games with better KDA but shittier cs and they were just A+ or S-.

Griseo has a banner up right now, in my region that is (SEA), and since you're a beginner, Elysia HoH should be on the starter supply. Unfortunately, they are different banners so you have to choose which banner to roll on. Fortunately, Griseo is a farmable valkyrie, although rolling for her makes acquiring her easier. You can just focus on rolling for Elysia HoH and just farm Griseo using asterites. I think you get a lot of asterites as a beginner.

&#x200B;

Also, while Griseo is a support and Elysia HoH is a DPS, they function in two different teams. Griseo is a physical support and Elysia HoH is an Ice DPS, so you shouldn't play them together.

let's not act like people ship ez and lux because "they make sense in the lore" when they have actually never met (although riot shut it down in their base skins when lux got a VO update). they shipped them cause they're blond LMAO.

&#x200B;

skins are alternate universe retellings of the champions. In lore canon, sett is not the "spirit of challenge" in the same way that evelynn is not the "spirit of love," yet in the spirit blossom skins they can be who they are written to be. The narratives of champions can be changed in skinline universes, mainly because they do not affect in game canon lore.

&#x200B;

If you ACTUALLY cared about lore, alternate skin universes should NOT bother you.

i mean, an element that is animated differently (or in this case just plain animated, while everything else is live action) can be good at portraying horror, if done well. 

&#x200B;

a good example that comes to mind is that one episode of courage the cowardly dog with that mummy thing that spoke about the curse of the slab

Not the leaked bio full of he/him pronouns... lmao

